If you are trying to complete this boss for the bestiary, watch [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=i4cnYrzK30Q this video].
| behaviour      = 
| speed          = ?
| strategy       = You can only fight this boss in teams of four. A balanced setup consists of 1 knight and 3 others to act as damage dealers.

The Ravager begins the fight alongside 4 [[Greater Canopic Jar]]s and is capable of summoning additional [[Canopic Jar]]s throughout the encounter. These jars remain stationary, but if The Ravager is moved too far away from them, he will summon new jars closer to his current position. Because of this mechanic, controlling the boss's positioning is essential.

At the start of the fight, the shooters should quickly destroy all [[Greater Canopic Jar]]s while the knight manipulates The Ravager's movement to gather the regular [[Canopic Jar]]s into a single area. Once the jars have been grouped together, the knight must position The Ravager just outside the jars' healing range while remaining close enough to prevent them from despawning.

After the setup is complete, the team should focus entirely on trapping and killing The Ravager. Do not allow him to move out of position, as this may cause him to regain access to healing or summon additional jars. Ideally, the knight should stand diagonally adjacent to The Ravager while trapping him with [[Wild Growth Rune]]s or [[Magic Wall Rune]]s. The shooters should remain positioned behind the knight to prevent the boss from escaping the trap and targeting other party members.
| location       = [[Oramond]], south in the [[Oramond Catacombs]].
